    <div itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer">
      <div itemprop="text">
        <p>Yes. In the Instapaper iOS app (version 10+), tap the "..." menu next to any article and select "Download EPUB." The file downloads to your phone, and you can then share it to your e-reader's app (Kindle, Kobo) or transfer via USB. The rebuilt web platform in Instapaper 10 also supports EPUB export directly from the browser.</p>
